# Calculator, Edit > Paste in the scientific view: "((1+2)*3@-2#)%7+4!=" (parentheses, x^2, x^3,
# Mod, n!), then typed 5 and the same text pasted again
# Port side: the text goes onto the clipboard with "clip"; the reference frames come from
# calc-paste2.scn (Program Manager shell, Notepad copies the text; its frames before
# Calculator pastes are not compared, only those of Calculator's window); recorded with
# dosbox-x_MinGWx64_SDL2.exe (its FPU computes with the host x87, as a real 387 would).
# regress: ARCH311_APP=apps/build/calc sh tools/run-cp-test.sh "$TEST" "$OUT"
# compare: calc-paste2/01.png 01.png active ignore 320 240 332 260
# compare: calc-paste2/02.png 02.png active ignore 320 240 332 260
# compare: calc-paste2/03.png 03.png active ignore 320 240 332 260
# compare: calc-paste2/04.png 04.png active ignore 320 240 332 260
# compare: calc-paste2/05.png 05.png active ignore 320 240 332 260
# ini: WIN.INI SciCalc layout=0
sleep 400
sleep 400
shot shots/01.png
key alt
key v
key s
sleep 400
shot shots/02.png
clip ((1+2)*3@-2#)%7+4!=
key alt
key e
key p
sleep 400
shot shots/03.png
key 5
sleep 400
shot shots/04.png
key alt
key e
key p
sleep 400
shot shots/05.png
